5,10.972L-46.719,11.045L-46.578,11.274L-46.477,11.248L-46.538,11.415L-46.379,11.612L-46.477,11.501L-46.477,11.57L-46.567,11.513L-46.654,11.612L-46.458,11.853L-46.477,11.965L-46.262,12.097L-46.094,12.591L-45.673,12.91L-45.678,13.301L-45.493,13.501L-45.494,13.643L-45.221,14.021L-45.221,14.21L-45.326,14.172L-45.358,14.232L-45.378,14.802L-45.17,14.937L-44.239,16.895L-43.643,17.784L-43.394,18.284L-43.255,18.736L-43.079,18.985L-42.373,20.418L-42.337,20.705L-42.162,20.871L-42.03,21.257L-41.884,21.479L-41.929,21.718L-41.811,21.765L-41.669,22.04L-41.22,22.417L-41.115,22.728L-40.928,22.975L-40.88,22.968L-40.899,22.874L-40.657,23.081L-40.609,23.265L-40.227,23.379L-40.072,23.639L-40.193,23.542L-40.382,23.611L-40.628,23.552L-40.871,23.399L-40.957,23.589L-40.983,23.974L-40.881,24.108L-40.941,24.941L-40.774,25.272L-40.696,25.854L-40.467,26.3L-40.351,26.755L-40.155,26.953L-40.27,26.756L-40.178,26.787L-40.094,27.073L-39.804,27.386L-38.829,27.708L-38.645,27.924L-38.579,28.17L-38.25,28.381L-38.217,28.604L-37.864,28.796L-37.432,29.206L-37.235,29.221L-37.132,29.399L-36.911,29.537L-36.921,29.727L-52.561,29.764L-52.399,29.193L-52.488,29.057L-52.596,29.02L-52.778,29.145L-53.097,29.767L-71.06,29.764ZM-45.339,14.364L-45.223,14.487L-45.2,14.626L-45.339,14.364ZM-45.063,12.248L-45.335,12.069L-45.4,12.1L-45.458,12.007L-45.313,11.974L-45.128,12.077L-45.063,12.248ZM-43.111,10.738L-43.313,10.701L-43.256,10.61L-43.112,10.615L-43.111,10.738ZM-43.793,10.515L-43.746,10.432L-43.677,10.451L-43.65,10.49L-43.768,10.556L-43.562,10.567L-43.432,10.733L-43.725,10.701L-43.793,10.515ZM-47.213,0.148L-46.712,0.386L-47.303,0.145L-47.213,0.148ZM-47.782,0.113L-48.263,0.366L-48.23,0.317L-47.776,0.07L-47.324,0.123L-47.782,0.113Z", "events": [{"year": -460, "title": "Inaros rises", "text": "Inaros, son of Psammetichus and a Libyan prince from Marea, raises Egypt in revolt against Artaxerxes I.", "lon": -57.65, "lat": -0.873}, {"year": -460, "title": "Sais joins", "text": "The old royal city of Sais and the western Delta rally to Inaros.", "lon": -54.468, "lat": -0.97}, {"year": -460, "title": "Amyrtaeus", "text": "An Egyptian leader, Amyrtaeus, fights alongside Inaros from the marshes of the western Delta.", "lon": -55.385, "lat": -0.038}, {"year": -460, "title": "Tribute stopped", "text": "The rebels drive out the Persian tribute collectors from the Delta, Diodorus says.", "lon": -53.952, "lat": -1.484}, {"year": -460, "title": "Call to Athens", "text": "Inaros asks Athens for help; the Athenians divert their fleet of 200 ships from Cyprus to Egypt.", "lon": -56.475, "lat": 0.219}, {"year": -460, "title": "Achaemenes comes", "text": "Achaemenes, satrap of Egypt and brother of Xerxes, leads a Persian army into the Delta.", "lon": -49.366, "lat": -0.713}, {"year": -460, "title": "Battle of Papremis", "text": "Inaros defeats and kills Achaemenes at Papremis, in the Delta; the exact site is unknown.", "lon": -53.522, "lat": -1.323}, {"year": -459, "title": "Up the Nile", "text": "Athenian triremes sail up the river from the sea and command the Nile.", "lon": -54.096, "lat": -2.608}, {"year": -459, "title": "Memphis taken", "text": "Athenians and rebels capture two of the three parts of Memphis, Egypt's capital.", "lon": -53.092, "lat": -4.535}, {"year": -459, "title": "The White Fortress", "text": "Persians, Medes and loyal Egyptians hold out in the White Fortress, Memphis's citadel.", "lon": -53.064, "lat": -4.567}, {"year": -459, "title": "Mendes joins", "text": "Mendes, chief city of the north-eastern Delta, is lost to the Persians.", "lon": -52.318, "lat": -0.97}, {"year": -459, "title": "Herodotus's skulls", "text": "Herodotus later saw the bones of the Persian dead still lying on the field of Papremis.", "lon": -53.465, "lat": -1.387}, {"year": -459, "title": "Coptos stays loyal", "text": "Persian officials at Coptos keep dating their inscriptions by Artaxerxes's reign.", "lon": -48.621, "lat": -16.933}, {"year": -458, "title": "Masters of the river", "text": "Athenian triremes control the Nile and its Delta branches, Thucydides says.", "lon": -53.522, "lat": -2.929}, {"year": -458, "title": "Siege drags on", "text": "The siege of the White Fortress settles into a long blockade.", "lon": -53.121, "lat": -4.471}, {"year": -458, "title": "Elephantine holds", "text": "At Elephantine, Persia's frontier garrison of Judean and Aramaean soldiers stays at its post.", "lon": -48.392, "lat": -23.036}, {"year": -458, "title": "Fleet at Prosopitis", "text": "The Athenian ships moor at the island of Prosopitis, a sheltered base between two Nile branches.", "lon": -54.21, "lat": -2.222}, {"year": -457, "title": "Megabyzus chosen", "text": "Artaxerxes sends Megabyzus, son of Zopyrus, and Artabazus to raise a new army in Syria and Cilicia.", "lon": -44.637, "lat": -0.038}, {"year": -457, "title": "A fleet is built", "text": "Cyprus, Phoenicia and Cilicia are ordered to build and man some 300 warships for Egypt.", "lon": -49.796, "lat": 0.122}, {"year": -457, "title": "The Delta waits", "text": "For a year the Persian army trains in Cilicia while the siege of Memphis continues.", "lon": -53.809, "lat": -2.126}, {"year": -456, "title": "Across Sinai", "text": "Megabyzus's army marches along the coast road from Syria into Egypt.", "lon": -47.503, "lat": -0.52}, {"year": -456, "title": "Pelusium", "text": "Army and fleet meet at Pelusium, the eastern gate of Egypt.", "lon": -49.366, "lat": -0.713}, {"year": -456, "title": "Battle near Memphis", "text": "Megabyzus defeats the Egyptians and their Greek allies in a pitched battle.", "lon": -52.949, "lat": -3.893}, {"year": -456, "title": "Memphis relieved", "text": "The White Fortress is freed and the Greeks are driven out of Memphis.", "lon": -53.092, "lat": -4.535}, {"year": -456, "title": "Inaros wounded", "text": "Ctesias says Megabyzus himself wounded Inaros in the thigh.", "lon": -53.379, "lat": -3.411}, {"year": -456, "title": "To Prosopitis", "text": "The Athenians fall back to the island of Prosopitis, between two branches of the Nile.", "lon": -54.153, "lat": -2.126}, {"year": -455, "title": "Siege of Prosopitis", "text": "Megabyzus besieges the Athenians and their fleet on the island for eighteen months.", "lon": -54.239, "lat": -2.287}, {"year": -455, "title": "Rebels melt away", "text": "Egyptian allies come to terms with the Persians and abandon the Athenians, Diodorus says.", "lon": -53.952, "lat": -1.644}, {"year": -455, "title": "Digging canals", "text": "Persian workers dig new channels to divert the river around the island.", "lon": -54.382, "lat": -2.447}, {"year": -454, "title": "Ships on dry land", "text": "The channel runs dry; the Athenian triremes are left stranded on the mud.", "lon": -54.182, "lat": -2.19}, {"year": -454, "title": "Island stormed", "text": "The Persians cross on foot and take the island, Thucydides says.", "lon": -54.096, "lat": -2.062}, {"year": -454, "title": "Ships burned", "text": "In Diodorus's version, the Athenians burn their own ships and leave under a truce.", "lon": -54.296, "lat": -2.287}, {"year": -454, "title": "Surrender at Byblos", "text": "Ctesias says Inaros and over six thousand Greeks surrendered at a stronghold called Byblos.", "lon": -53.809, "lat": -1.805}, {"year": -454, "title": "Inaros taken", "text": "Inaros is betrayed and captured; he is later impaled in Persia.", "lon": -53.952, "lat": -1.933}, {"year": -454, "title": "Through the desert", "text": "A few survivors escape west through the Libyan desert to Cyrene.", "lon": -64.586, "lat": 0.283}, {"year": -454, "title": "Mendesian mouth", "text": "Fifty Athenian and allied triremes, unaware of the fall, sail into the Mendesian mouth of the Nile.", "lon": -51.659, "lat": 0.443}, {"year": -454, "title": "Phoenician trap", "text": "Persian infantry from the shore and the Phoenician fleet destroy most of the relief squadron.", "lon": -51.373, "lat": 0.604}, {"year": -454, "title": "King in the marshes", "text": "Amyrtaeus escapes capture in the vast western marshes.", "lon": -54.955, "lat": -0.199}, {"year": -454, "title": "Egypt reconquered", "text": "After six years of war, Egypt is again a Persian province.", "lon": -53.092, "lat": -4.375}], "eras": [[-460, -460, "The Revolt of Inaros"], [-459, -457, "The Siege of Memphis"], [-456, -455, "The Trap at Prosopitis"], [-454, -454, "Disaster on the Nile"]], "refLine": null, "metrics": [{"label": "Held by rebels & Athenians", "stages": [1]}, {"label": "Persian-held or retaken", "stages": [0, 3]}], "chartNote": "Share of the area of modern Egypt, by who controlled each present-day governorate; regions are today's boundaries. A simplification: the sources name few places, the chronology of 460–454 BC is reconstructed, and the vast desert governorates make Persian-held land look larger than the populated Delta and Nile valley where the war was fought.", "chartTitle": "Control of Egypt by area", "shares": [[0.8103, 0.1795, 0.0102, 0.0], [0.7693, 0.1897, 0.041, 0.0], [0.7693, 0.1897, 0.041, 0.0], [0.7693, 0.1897, 0.041, 0.0], [0.7693, 0.1761, 0.0081, 0.0465], [0.7693, 0.1761, 0.0081, 0.0465], [0.7693, 0.0, 0.1761, 0.0546]], "seaTile": "data:image/svg+xml;base64,", "theme": {"--sea": "#14304A", "--sea-deep": "#0B1D2E", "--shade": "10,20,30", "--neighbor": "#2E4556", "--neighbor-edge": "#5B7385", "--glaze": "#F8F2E8", "--gold": "#B9863F", "--gold-bright": "#DDAE62", "--accent": "#6B1F4E", "--accent-hover": "#842862", "--ink": "#1E1A22", "--ink-muted": "#625A66", "--paper": "#F2EBDF", "--font-display": "'Marcellus', 'Noto Serif', 'DejaVu Serif', 'Noto Sans CJK JP', Georgia, serif", "--font-body": "'Cardo', 'Noto Serif', 'DejaVu Serif', 'Noto Sans CJK JP', Georgia, serif", "--cobalt": "#14304A", "--cobalt-deep": "#0B1D2E", "--wine": "#6B1F4E"}}